# ============================================================================
# FlowAblation / ablating sharp wedge in a Mach 3 viscous stream  (Hydro2, ablation.on = 1)
#
# NON-DEFORMING embedded body.  15 deg half-angle wedge, tip at x = -0.5, in a Mach 3
# stream (rho 1, p 0.714, gamma 1.4 -> c = 1, U = 3; mu 2e-3 -> Re = 1500 per unit length;
# Pr 0.72).  No-slip isothermal wall at the free-stream temperature T_inf = p/(rho R) =
# 2.4876e-3 (R = cp - cv = 287.14); stagnation temperature T0 = 2.8 T_inf.
# Heat-of-ablation model: rho_s Q* v = q_w with rho_s = 1, Q* = 80, no acceleration factor
# (ablation.accel = 1), recession starts at t = 1.
# The laminar wall heat flux scales like 1/sqrt(distance from the leading edge), so the tip
# recedes fastest and BLUNTS; once it has a nose radius the stagnation-point heat flux
# falls like 1/sqrt(R_nose) and the recession slows.  No closed form for the shape.
# 800 x 480 cells (dx = 0.0025), single level (ablation is single-level so far).
#
# Run (from bin/): mpirun -np 16 ./hydro2-2d-g++ ../tests/FlowAblation/UNIT_TEST_2D_Wedge plot_file=<dir>/output
# Check:           python3 ../tests/FlowAblation/reference/ablation_wedge_check.py <dir>
# ============================================================================
